  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal/multiprofile/scvi_n200/resnet50/avgpool/concat at 0.632 acc), the evidence is very sparse. The most informative single-axis change is upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while holding all other factors constant (config_042). This directly tests whether a stronger visual backbone is the primary bottleneck, which would guide whether subsequent experiments should invest in heavier encoders or instead focus on aggregation/fusion/RNA-encoder choices. If ViT-L yields a meaningful accuracy gain, it validates the direction of stronger encoders for the remaining 8 experiments; if not, it redirects effort toward aggregation (transformer) or RNA-encoder (scgpt/pca_n2000) improvements. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_001 (~14–18 GPU hrs vs 7.27) due to ViT-L's larger parameter count, but still manageable within the remaining budget and well below the cost of combining ViT-L with transformer aggregation."
}

